  <h2>Cleanliness & A Healthy Living Environment</h2>

  <p>
    Cleanliness is one of the most important aspects of maintaining
    your cat's health and wellbeing. A clean living environment helps
    reduce unpleasant odours, limit the buildup of bacteria, and
    create a comfortable space where your cat can rest, eat, drink,
    and feel secure.
  </p>

  <p>
    Cats are naturally clean animals, and maintaining their litter
    area, drinking water, and favourite resting places is an essential
    part of responsible everyday care.
  </p>

  <h3>Maintaining a Clean Litter Box</h3>

  <p>
    Remove waste from the litter box daily and replace the litter
    completely every one to two weeks, depending on the type of litter,
    the number of cats, and how quickly it becomes soiled. Wash and
    thoroughly dry the litter box before adding fresh litter. A clean
    litter area encourages good habits and helps prevent unpleasant
    odours.
  </p>

