  <h3>Washing Blankets & Bedding</h3>

  <p>
    Your cat's favourite blankets and bedding can collect loose fur,
    dust, dirt, and other debris. Wash blankets and washable bedding
    regularly, using a gentle, fragrance-free detergent when possible.
    Make sure everything is completely dry before returning it to
    your cat's resting area.
  </p>

  <h3>A Simple Cleaning Routine</h3>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Daily:</strong> Remove waste from the litter box and provide fresh drinking water.</li>
    <li><strong>Every 3–6 days:</strong> Clean the water fountain and check its filter.</li>
    <li><strong>Every 1–2 weeks:</strong> Replace the litter completely and wash the litter box.</li>
    <li><strong>Regularly:</strong> Wash blankets, bedding, and other washable items your cat uses.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Consistent cleaning habits make a meaningful difference in your
    cat's everyday comfort. By keeping their surroundings fresh,
    hygienic, and well maintained, you help create a healthier home
    for your feline companion.
  </p>
